<%- include('_partials/head') %>
<%- include('_partials/nav') %>

<main class="container page-container">
    <section class="page-header-center">
        <div class="badge-pill">Conversation-first coordination</div>
        <h1 class="page-title">How Kurukoo Works</h1>
        <p class="page-desc">Kurukoo is a conversational fulfilment network with native personal assistance, a provider and inventory network, controlled external execution, and a bounded autonomous goal runtime. It does not promise a provider, payment, dispatch or fulfilment until the applicable evidence and integration boundary are confirmed.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="how-it-works-grid">
        <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-number">01</div>
            <h3>Tell Kurukoo what you need</h3>
            <p>Start in Web Chat and describe the need in plain language. Kurukoo keeps the request in context without asking you to repeat it after a required sign-in step.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-number">02</div>
            <h3>Kurukoo assesses the request</h3>
            <p>Kurukoo identifies the relevant request path and checks whether the underlying skill, provider or inventory data, bounded goal follow-up, or connector support is available.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-number">03</div>
            <h3>Review a supported next step</h3>
            <p>A provider, quote, or offer is presented only when its underlying data and authorization boundary are available.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-number">04</div>
            <h3>Confirm eligible actions</h3>
            <p>Protected actions request identity when necessary. Controlled external execution, payment, escrow, delivery and fulfilment steps appear only where their verified integrations and evidence are available.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="kurukoo-ad-placement" data-kurukoo-ad-placement="how_it_works_inline" data-country="<%= market.code %>" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Sponsored content"></div>

    <section class="how-it-works-cta">
        <div class="cta-box">
            <h2>Ready to get started?</h2>
            <p>Start a conversation and Kurukoo will show the supported path for the request.</p>
            <a href="/chat" class="btn btn-primary">Start chatting</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>

<style>
.how-it-works-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: 32px;
    margin: 60px 0;
}
.step-card {
    padding: 32px;
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    position: relative;
}
.step-number {
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--terracotta);
    opacity: 0.15;
    position: absolute;
    top: 10px;
    right: 20px;
}
.how-it-works-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 80px 0;
    background: var(--gray-50);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);
}
.cta-box h2 { margin-bottom: 16px; }
.cta-box p { margin-bottom: 32px; color: var(--gray-600); }
</style>

<%- include('_partials/footer') %>
